   301	### The magnitude does not transfer across providers
   302	
   303	Measured on Vertex with `gemini-3-flash-preview`, **within a single grid** (original
   304	environment, output cap 600, reasoning budget 0, n=5 episodes per cell) so that the
   305	comparison is not mixing conditions. The figure is cache-read tokens over total input
   306	tokens:
   307	
   308	| Runtime | T=25 | T=50 | T=100 | T=200 |
   309	|---|---|---|---|---|
   310	| ReAct | 1.1 % | 4.6 % | 6.8 % | **7.0 %** |
   311	| Stateful | 0 % | 2.6 % | 4.3 % | 4.3 % |
   312	| Memory, SKILL.state | 0 % | 0 % | 0 % | 0 % |
   313	
   314	Implicit caching therefore **exists on Vertex and favours exactly the arms whose prefix
   315	is append-only**, growing with the horizon — the same qualitative pattern as Anthropic,
   316	an order of magnitude smaller: **7 % against 82 %**. Other grids in other conditions give
   317	between 1 % and 16 % for ReAct; the spread across conditions is not characterised here.
   318	
   319	Paired within that grid, the cost ratio barely moves:
   320	
   321	| | Raw input | Effective input |
   322	|---|---|---|
   323	| T=50, ReAct / SKILL.state | 7.90x | **7.57x** |
   324	| T=200, ReAct / SKILL.state | 29.16x | **27.32x** |
   325	
   326	A direct probe adds nuance and a warning. Repeating an identical 13,346-token request,
   327	one run read 12,262 cached tokens on the second call and a later run read none; issuing
   328	eight calls whose prefix grows by ~3,300 tokens each, none read any. Implicit caching is
   329	**opportunistic and not reproducible on demand**: our probes of the growing-prefix
   330	pattern registered nothing while the grids of that same pattern registered 7 %. We report
   331	the grid figures, which are the ones the experiment actually incurred. Probe outputs are
   332	persisted in `results/probe_cache_vertex_*.json`.
   333	
   334	> An earlier version of this section stated that Vertex has no implicit cache. It was
   335	> wrong: it generalised from the identical-request probe, and the project's own grids
   336	> contradicted it — 503,600 cached tokens in a single ReAct episode at T=200. A clean
   337	> measurement of the wrong thing.
   338	
   339	Explicit caching works (20,013 of 20,016 tokens discounted, and 13,343 of 13,346 in a
   340	second run) but does not fit ReAct's pattern: its prefix grows every step, so an object
   341	cached at step *k* covers a shrinking fraction of the prompt at step *k+n*. We did not
   342	measure whether repeatedly rebuilding it pays off; the claim here is only that the
   343	naive use — one fixed cached block — does not apply.
   344	
   345	Resulting statement: **prefix caching helps only the append-only arms, in both providers,
   346	and by an order of magnitude more on Anthropic. The inversion of the accounting we
   347	measured there does not reproduce on Vertex, where 7.9x in tokens remains 7.6x in
   348	effective input.**
