   352	## 5. Two probes on their declared limitations
   353	
   354	The paper declares two limitations without measuring them. We measured them.
   355	
   376	
   377	### L2: retroactive invalidation
   378	
   379	An announced fact stops being true later. Counted over **dependent steps**, not
   380	episodes:
   381	
   382	| Model | Runtime | Applies the correction |
   383	|---|---|---|
   384	| Haiku 4.5 | ReAct | 3/44 — 6.8 % |
   385	| Haiku 4.5 | SKILL.state | **44/44 — 100 %** |
   386	| Sonnet 5 | ReAct | 15/38 — 39.5 % |
   387	| Sonnet 5 | SKILL.state | **49/49 — 100 %** |
   388	
   389	**Explicit state does not fail once: 93 of 93 dependent steps.** Full history gets 18 of
   390	82. Two conditions of that count, from the source measurement: episodes with more than
   391	three truncated responses are excluded (six Sonnet/ReAct episodes), and the SKILL.state
   392	column counts only the dependent steps — the same runs recorded 21 other failures, 10
   393	steps with no action and 66 invalid patches in Sonnet. The 100 % characterises
   394	retroactive invalidation, **not** the runtime's overall reliability. And ReAct's
   395	failure is all-or-nothing per scenario: in Haiku it misses all 11 dependent steps of one
   396	episode, all 7 of another, all 4 of a third. This is not an agent that slips; it is a
   397	flawless agent that **never updated a fact**.
   398	
   399	### Both probes on the third model
   400	
   401	Repeated on `gemini-3-flash-preview` via Vertex. **L1** uses the same output cap and
   402	reasoning budget as Table 1 (8192 / 0), 3 seeds × 8 repetitions per cell. **L2** uses cap
   403	8192 with the provider's default reasoning — its runner does not expose the budget flag —
   404	and 3 seeds × 2 repetitions:
   405	
   406	| L1 condition | ReAct | SKILL.state |
   407	|---|---|---|
   408	| No field to store it | 0/24 = 0 % [0–14] | 0/24 = 0 % [0–14] |
   409	| Free-form `notes` field | 0/24 = 0 % [0–14] | **0/24 = 0 % [0–14]** |
   410	| Schema field naming the fact | 0/24 = 0 % [0–14] | **16/24 = 67 % [47–82]** |
   411	| Reminder on the observation | **16/24 = 67 % [47–82]** | 8/24 = 33 % [18–53] |
   412	
   413	The floor is **zero in every run**, where in Claude it was a noisy 12 %; its Wilson
   414	interval still admits up to 14 %, so "zero" describes the sample, not the population. The
   415	intervals of the working conditions do not overlap it. Three things follow, with one
   416	caveat stated first: **the successes concentrate by scenario, not by trial.** Per seed,
   417	SKILL.state with the schema field scores 0/8, 8/8, 8/8, and with the reminder 0/8, 8/8,
   418	0/8. Binomial intervals over 24 runs do not capture the uncertainty of generalising to
   419	new scenarios, and the 67 %-vs-33 % difference between those two conditions comes
   420	entirely from one seed.
   421	
   422	- **The free-form field fails in both models.** 0/24 in Gemini, indistinguishable from
   423	  having no field at all. The recommendation this project once made and then withdrew
   424	  ("leave a hatch in your schema") finds no support in either model.
   425	- **Naming the field works** (67 %), reproducing L1: explicit state protects what its
   426	  designer anticipated.
   427	- **The reminder works for the runtime that has nowhere to store anything.** ReAct with
   428	  the fact attached to the observation reaches the same 67 % that SKILL.state reaches
   429	  with a dedicated schema field. For SKILL.state the reminder scores lower than its own
   430	  schema field (33 % against 67 %), but that gap rests on a single seed and we do not
   431	  claim it.
   432	
   433	L2 on the same model, counted over dependent steps:
   434	
   435	| Model | ReAct applies the correction | SKILL.state |
   436	|---|---|---|
   437	| Haiku 4.5 | 3/44 | 44/44 |
   438	| Sonnet 5 | 8/44 | 44/44 |
   439	| **Gemini 3 Flash** | **0/44** | **44/44** |
   440	
   441	**132 of 132 dependent steps with explicit state, across three models and three
   442	services, against 11 of 132 with full history.**
   443	
   444	Gemini is the model that never updates a fact — 0 of 44 — while scoring 0.913 on the
   445	long procedure. Haiku, measured now under the same conditions as Gemini's Table 1 (§3),
   446	scores **0.974** on that procedure at T=200 and still misses 41 of 44 corrections. The two
   447	L2 measurements do not share every setting (§7), so we do not rank the models on it;
   448	what holds on both is that **the long-procedure score does not predict this failure, and
   449	within each model the runtime decides it.**
   562	- **`gemini-3-flash-preview` may not be their `Gemini-3-Flash`.** Declared as a risk
   563	  from the outset. Vertex returns the responding model ID on every call and it is
   564	  recorded per step, but not in the traces measured before that change. The Anthropic
   565	  client did not copy it until the last Stateful re-measurement: from then on — its 30
   566	  episodes and the prompt-order experiment — every step records
   567	  `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`; the earlier Haiku traces record only the requested alias
   568	  in their header.
   569	- **A reimplemented environment is not their environment.** We matched what their
   570	  appendix allows us to compare, and the remaining differences are in §2. The shelf
   571	  choice in `Store` still awaits an answer from the authors.
   572	- **Our Memory is not comparable to theirs.** Our summariser compresses fourteen times
   573	  more (5,770-token mean prompt against their 84,364 at T=200).
   574	  What we measured is our summarisation policy, not "summarisation" as a category.
   575	- **We have not proven the environment gaps have no effect**; we measured that, at the
   576	  power available, none above ~5 points is detectable. The same caveat applies to the
   577	  three lowest noise levels in §3.
   578	- **Cell sizes are not uniform.** Nineteen cells carry 15 runs; ReAct at T=200 carries
   579	  19, unbalanced across seeds (3/3/7/3/3). Five of its episodes exist only as
   580	  aggregates, without traces.
   581	- **Cost figures price input only**, and the caching results depend on the length of the
   582	  static prefix (§4).
   583	- **The probes now cover all three models**, across three services (Vertex, the
   584	  Anthropic API and Microsoft Foundry), but not under identical settings: L1 on Gemini
   585	  fixes the reasoning budget at 0 to match Table 1; L2 uses the provider default because
   586	  its runner does not expose the flag; and the Claude runs predate that control. Their
   587	  counts carry the exclusions listed in §5.
   588	- **One environment.** The second (Software Repository) was retired: it did not
   589	  discriminate between runtimes and would have added noise without information.
   590	- **SKILL.state's ceiling depends on the model.** At 1.000 with zero variance on Gemini
   591	  the task did not discriminate at the top; on Haiku it does (0.958 at T=200), and the
   592	  failure is in writing the state (§3). Two models are not enough to say which models
   593	  make that error.
   594	- **Stateful has been re-measured only at T=50 and T=200**, with parser version 2 on
   595	  Gemini (which applied 3,748 of 3,750 of its patches) and version 3 on Haiku. The
   596	  intermediate horizons of Gemini's Table 1 keep the defective measurement, marked as
   597	  such.
   598	- **Haiku and Gemini do not share decoding settings** (§3): the cross-model differences
   599	  are between two configured systems, not two models under identical conditions.
   600	- **Haiku's Memory column mixes the summarisation policy with summary truncation** (§3);
   601	  the control arm has n=9 and bounds the effect at T=50 only.
